body:
You may have overwritten an ActiveAdmin Sass predefined color.  Here's a list of the ones I found, still digging to find the actual ones that your color are.

``` scss
// Variables used throughout Active Admin

// Colors
$primary-color: #5E6469;
$secondary-color: #f0f0f0;
$text-color: #323537;
$link-color: #38678b;
$section-header-text-color: $primary-color;
$current-menu-item-background: lighten($primary-color, 12%);
$hover-menu-item-background: lighten($primary-color, 12%);
$table-stripe-color: lighten($primary-color, 57%); 
$table-selected-color: #d9e4ec;
$error-color: #932419;

// Sizes
$horizontal-page-margin: 30px;
$sidebar-width: 270px;
$cell-padding: 5px 10px 3px 10px;
$cell-horizontal-padding: 12px;
$section-padding: 15px;
$text-input-horizontal-padding: 10px;
```

The only SASS I have are custom `status_tag` colors and this:

``` sass
//remove this if ActiveAdmin issue # 974 is ever fixed
#header {
  position: inherit;
}
```

#974 being that drop-down menus don't work properly in Internet Explorer

edit: going back to that issue, I see you're the one who started it ^^'
edit edit: turns out that's not the problem... Even after removing my SASS, the buttons stayed blue!

@oldtinroof Thanks for the suggestion, but I haven't defined any gradients.

@jancel The only CSS I've added myself is in `active_admin.css.scss`, and that's definitely making it to the browser.

I don't know what to do. I tried `git checkout` to go back to previous versions of my code, as well as to go back to the beginning of 0.4.3 for ActiveAdmin. I temporarily erased the little SASS I have, and erased everything in `./tmp/`. I uninstalled all of my gems multiple times, and yet this is still an issue!

The next thing to try is to do a clean install of Ruby itself (I use RVM)....
